Licensing scope

CC0 1.0 Universal (licenses/CC0-1.0.txt): the reconstructions under reconstruction/, the
documentation, research notes, reports and data that this project authored. Contributors
dedicate their contributions the same way, unless a file states an exception below.

MIT (licenses/MIT.txt): original project-authored infrastructure in tools/, tests/, site/,
.github/, and the original .gitignore and .gitattributes. Unchanged by the CC0 dedication.

Exceptions inside the CC0 scope. These are decided per file, by rule, and CC0 cannot cover them:
- Units carrying a third-party SPDX line (`SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT (CommonLibSSE-NG ...)`,
  `GPL-3.0-or-later`, `GPL-3.0-only`) keep that licence and its notice. This includes every unit
  whose header declares GPL-3.0 declarations or labels (COMMUNITY(powerof3/CommonLibSSE@..., GPL-3.0),
  the powerof3 or CommonLibSSE-GPL notice, or a GPL header block): such a unit stays GPL-3.0
  (full text: licenses/CommonLibSSE-GPL-3.0.txt). CommonLibSSE-NG declarations stay MIT
  (licenses/CommonLibSSE-NG.txt).
- Units labelled SIBLING(fo4-private@1b765c70, author-permission): use was permitted by that
  work's author; it is not dedicated under CC0 and no relicence is granted for it.
- Material labelled SIBLING(momusdigital/fnv_decomp@...) is taken from a project that is itself
  CC0 1.0, so it carries no exception; the label stays for provenance.
A unit with no SPDX line and none of the markers above is CC0. New units carry
`// SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0`.

Not covered: Skyrim, its code, executables, assets and trademarks, middleware and any other
third-party material are not licensed by this project. CC0 grants no rights in Bethesda's
intellectual property or in anyone else's; it dedicates only what the project's authors can
dedicate. Nothing here asserts that the maintainer owns third-party rights. All future third-party
additions require an explicit license and attribution record.
